            "Hexagonal system. Short to elongated hexagonal prisms with flat terminations. Imperfect basal cleavage; conchoidal fracture. Hardness 7.5 to 8; specific gravity 2.60 to 2.90 depending on alkali content; vitreous lustre; refractive index 1.566 to 1.602; birefringence 0.004 to 0.008 (uniaxial negative). Being colourless, it shows no visible pleochroism. Its low dispersion gives it little fire: once cut, it shines with a crisp, sober brilliance. It was once used to imitate diamond and emerald, backed with coloured metal foil.",
            "United States: Goshen (Massachusetts), the type locality, and Maine. Brazil (Minas Gerais), the main current source. Madagascar, Pakistan, Russia, Namibia, Canada and China. Large, perfectly transparent colourless crystals remain sought after by collectors.",
